% ==================== FIGURE / TABLE NUMBERING ====================
% Chapter-based figure AND table numbering: Figure 1.1 / Table 1.1, 1.2, ...
% Figures implement Rayman review item C1; tables follow the same convention so
% the Lua-emitted numbered \caption reads "Table C.N" and the List of Tables
% populates. The chapter counter still drives the N.M prefix even though chapter
% headings carry no visible number (secnumdepth = -1) -- the counter increments
% regardless, exactly as it already does for figures.
\counterwithin{figure}{chapter}
\counterwithin{table}{chapter}

